Hello all, long-time player, first-time poster here :)

"long-time" is relative, and it hasn't been that long, in fact I'm
quite a n00b despite my efforst to get a handle on the game.

But anyway, I have a bunch of nethack related things rattling around in
head I thought I'd post here.

Basically, I'm stuck.  I've done a few iterations on reading the
fantastic spoilers (I couldn't get far without 'em), and searching
through this wonderous newsgroup, but I think I've just hit a block of
some kind.  I'm playing the tiled Qt version of 3.4.1 on Cygwin "as is"
(I can't quite handle the character based version or I'd play on
nethack.alt.org).

Overall, I haven't really gotten farther than Sokoban and the bottom of
the mines.  But that's not really the problem.  Truth is that I'm
having problems playing the character I want to be able to play.
Here's how it's gone so far:

Wizard: This is the one I'd like to be able to play, but I typically
die by char level 9 before having completed both the mines and Sokoban
and getting Magicbaine.  It's almost certain that I lack the skill, but
I have tried following the advice I've read.  I typically play an
Elf-Wiz, but I've also tried Gnome (I had too much trouble with Human
early on due to lack of infravision and skill :).  I'm not sure what
anyone here can do since there's plenty of advice on the net, but I
just thought I'd share my pain :)

Barbarian/Orc: This is such a different experience from the Wizard that
it makes me laugh.  I can go pretty far (for me) and in much less time,
but then I get bored and die :)  Um, by "far" I mean clearing Sokoban
and the mines and then trying to get my kit together for the quest.

Healer/Gnome: I got pretty far as a healer playing the protection
raquet and then turning violent.  Using meatballs to train my pets
seemed like such a great idea, but by the time I could make a lot of
meatballs I didn't really need to train my pets.

Monk: I actually like playing the monk and I can get about as far as
the Barb with a bit more effort.  Then I still end up wishing I was a
Wizard.  Still, maybe it's a monk I should be playing.

Archeologist(Dwarf): I like this class, and recently I've been able to
get a bit farther than the Wizard.  The key seems to be better armor
and weapon early on (I go for the mattoch when I can), and then there
seems to be good spell casting potential later on which is appealing.
But the character still feels to fragile.  I probably level too fast.

I almost think I need an easier game so I can enjoy the Wizard.  It's
just been hard to get things to line up right.  Spell casting is a bit
more fun then bashing, and the spells themselves are tantalizing.  I
know some people consider the Wizard to be the easiest class to play,
but I really can't see how.  I've be putting in a lot of effort, but
I'm definitely missing it.

Thanks for listening/reading :)  Any comments, help or insight is
greatily appreciated.

